# Advanced layouts to code (Ignore auto layout)

## PRIORITY — read frame constraints before any size (mandatory)

**Before** writing `w-*`, `h-*`, `aspect-*`, `min-h-*`, or `flex-*` on a frame, open that node in Figma (Dev Mode / `get_metadata` + inspect sizing) and record **per axis**:

| Check in Figma | What to code |
| -------------- | ------------ |
| **Width / Height** mode: Hug, Fill, Fixed | Hug → intrinsic / omit fixed size; Fill → parent stretch (`flex-1`, `items-stretch`); Fixed → `w-[…]` / `h-[…]` in rem |
| **Aspect ratio** locked vs **unlock** | Locked → `aspect-[W/H]` only when Figma locks it; **Unlock → never `aspect-[W/H]` on that frame** |
| **Min / max** width or height | `min-h-*`, `max-w-*`, etc. from those values (rem) |
| **Constraints** panel (Scale, pin, stretch) | See [Constraint → CSS](#constraint--css) below |

**Do not** derive container size from:

- `get_design_context` class strings (`aspect-[705/416]`, `h-[416px]`, `size-full`)
- Snapshot **W × H** in `get_metadata` (artboard dimensions at one breakpoint — not a ratio contract)
- Raw image intrinsic ratio

Codegen output is a **hint for structure and absolute children**, not for parent frame sizing. If you skip Figma constraints and copy MCP dimensions, you will re-break **Unlock + Fill** (CommunityInfo, WhatWeDo imagery, etc.).

```tsx
// Figma: what we do imagery — unlock aspect, W Fill, H Fill, min-h 416.849px
// ❌ NEVER — copied snapshot W÷H from metadata/codegen
<div className="relative aspect-[705.905/416.849] flex-1" />

// ✅ Read constraints first
<div className="relative min-h-[26.053rem] min-w-0 flex-1" />
// Parent row: items-stretch (not items-center)
```

**Workflow (every frame you size):** Figma constraints → rem values → CSS. MCP last, for absolute child offsets only.

---

A Figma child with **Ignore auto layout** is **out of flow**. Parent stays Auto Layout; that child is `absolute` against the parent’s padding box. Parent must be `relative` (or already positioned).

Do not put the ignored node in `flex`/`gap` with in-flow siblings. MCP `hypot()`, `cqw`, and extra rotate shells are codegen — keep **one** absolute node.

## Constraint → CSS

Read the **Constraints** panel (H and V separately). `%` is **of the parent size** on that axis. Negative `%`/`px` = hangs outside (overlap).

| Figma (axis)                 | CSS                                                                                                             |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Left** pin + fixed size    | `left-[Npx]`, `w-*` (or `h-*` on Y with `top`)                                                                  |
| **Right** pin + fixed size   | `right-[Npx]`, `w-*`                                                                                            |
| **Left and right** (stretch) | `left-*` + `right-*`, **no** fixed `w-*`                                                                        |
| **Scale**                    | `left-[N%]` **and** `right-[N%]`. Width is implied: `100% − left − right`. Do **not** replace with `w-[349px]`. |
| **Center**                   | `left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2` (Y: `top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2`)                                                     |
| **Top** / **Bottom** pin     | `top-[Npx]` / `bottom-[Npx]` — pins stay **px** if Figma used px                                                |
| **Scale** on Y               | `top-[N%]` **and** `bottom-[N%]`                                                                                |

Mix freely (this file’s close-up): **Scale X** + **Bottom** pin + **aspect** instead of height.

```tsx
// Scale X + bottom pin  →  width tracks parent; stays 3px from bottom
className = "absolute left-[-48%] right-[82%] bottom-[3px] aspect-[349/243]";

// ❌ WRONG — kills Scale; won’t track parent width
className = "absolute bottom-[3px] left-[-252px] w-[349px]";
```

`left: -48.27%` + `right: 81.62%` on a `524px` parent ≈ **349px** wide. Keep the **%** so it still holds if the parent changes.

## Image ratio & dimensions (not the raw file)

MCP often emits `aspect-[1125/750]` (or similar) from the **uploaded bitmap’s intrinsic size**. That is **not** the ratio to code unless the frame in Figma has no crop, mask, or fixed resize.

Use the **design frame** — what the user actually sees:

| Figma situation                                      | Code from                                                                                            |
| ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Mask** / clip / “Mask group”                       | `mask-size` (width × height of the visible area), or the masked frame’s W×H                          |
| **Unlock aspect ratio** + fixed W and H              | Independent `w-[…]` + `h-[…]` from the **frame**. Do **not** use `aspect-*` — that re-locks the axes |
| **Unlock aspect ratio** + **Fill** on an axis        | That axis comes from the parent layout (stretch/fill). Never invent `aspect-[W/H]` from the artboard snapshot |
| **Locked aspect ratio** + one dimension              | Frame aspect or the constrained axis from layout                                                     |
| Fill inside a rounded clip with no mask              | The **image layer / clip frame** size in the tree                                                    |

```tsx
// ❌ Raw download ratio (e.g. 1125×750 photo)
<div className="aspect-[1125/750] overflow-hidden rounded-[1rem]">
  <img src="/assets/seals/community.png" className="size-full object-cover" />
</div>

// ✅ Design mask-size 266×126.834 (large seal variant)
<div className="aspect-[266/126.834] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-[1rem]">
  <img src="/assets/seals/community.png" className="size-full object-cover" />
</div>

// ✅ Unlock aspect ratio — fixed frame 266×127 in Figma (both axes Hug/fixed)
<div className="h-[7.9275rem] w-[16.625rem] overflow-hidden rounded-[1rem]">
  <img src="..." className="size-full object-cover" />
</div>
```

`object-cover` fills the **design box**; the box size comes from Figma, not from `file dimensions` or MCP asset metadata.

## Fill height/width ≠ `h-full` / `w-full` (flex)

Figma **Fill** on the cross axis of an Auto Layout parent means: grow with the sibling row/column. In CSS that is **flex stretch**, not percentage size.

| Figma                         | CSS                                                                                                      |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Parent Auto Layout (row/col)  | `flex` + `items-stretch` (default stretch; don’t use `items-start`/`items-end` if a child must Fill)   |
| Child **Fill** height in a row | Keep `height: auto` (omit `h-*`). Stretch gives the used height. Optional: `self-stretch`              |
| Child **Fill** width in a col  | Keep `width: auto` / `w-auto`, or `flex-1` / `self-stretch` as appropriate — not blind `w-full`        |
| Child fixed on the other axis | e.g. Fill height + fixed width → `w-[32.75rem] shrink-0` + **no** `h-full`, **no** `aspect-*`          |

```tsx
// Parent row — stretch so Fill children can match the tallest sibling
<div className="flex items-stretch gap-20">
  <div className="flex flex-1 flex-col">{/* in-flow copy */}</div>

  {/* ✅ Unlock + Fill height: width fixed, height from stretch */}
  <div className="relative w-[32.75rem] shrink-0">
    {/* absolute children with Scale/pin % */}
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ WRONG — aspect re-locks unlocked axes; snapshot H is not a ratio contract
<div className="relative aspect-[524/465] w-[32.75rem]" />

// ❌ WRONG — h-full is height:100%; % needs a specified parent height.
// Flex parents sized by content are height:auto → % fails. Absolute kids add
// no intrinsic height → the box collapses to 0.
<div className="relative h-full w-[32.75rem]" />
```

**Why not `h-full`:** `height: 100%` only resolves if the parent has a **specified** height. A flex row whose height comes from content does not. `align-items: stretch` only applies when the item’s cross size is `auto`. Setting `h-full` leaves stretch and breaks Fill. Absolute-only children make the collapse obvious (empty red/debug box).

## Checks

- **First:** Figma frame sizing (Hug / Fill / Fixed, unlock aspect, min/max) — **not** MCP `aspect-*` or snapshot W×H.
- In-flow siblings: Auto Layout (`flex` + `gap`). Ignored sibling: `absolute` + constraints, not `order`/`gap`.
- `%` on `left`/`right` together → Scale (or stretch in %). Don’t “simplify” to px width.
- Pin in px → keep px. Don’t turn `bottom-[3px]` into `%` unless Figma is Scale on Y.
- Image `aspect-*` / `w`/`h` → from mask, clip frame, or unlocked W×H — never from the raw image file ratio.
- **Unlock aspect** → never encode W÷H as `aspect-*`. Fixed axes → independent `w`/`h`; Fill axis → flex stretch + `auto` size, **not** `h-full`/`w-full`.
- Fill child in a flex row/col → parent `items-stretch`; child omit cross-axis size (or `self-stretch`). Don’t pair Fill with `items-start`.
- Same node, different constraints per breakpoint → follow `ffs-figma-faithful-structure` (two trees), don’t blend Scale and pin on one element.
